== English ==

"The Software" means the JM-Orgue program as published by the author: the
official installers and everything they contain. "The source code" means the
code in this repository, which is published for reference only.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

  1. Use, install and run the Software, as often and on as many computers as
     you like, at home or in a church, privately or within an organisation.
     No permission is needed and there is no charge.

  2. Pass the Software on and distribute it freely: give it to others, put it
     on a website or forum, carry it on a USB stick, share it within a church
     or musical circle.

     Three conditions apply:
       a. you pass on the official installer unmodified, complete and as the
          author published it;
       b. you do not charge for it, and you do not charge for anything of
          which the Software forms part;
       c. this licence travels with it, you leave the author's name intact,
          and you do not present the Software as your own work.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO, without prior written permission from the author:

  1. sell, rent or sublicense the Software, or offer it for payment as part
     of a product or service;
  2. modify, unpack, rebuild or reverse engineer the Software or its
     installers;
  3. copy, modify, translate or create derivative works of the source code
     or parts of it;
  4. incorporate the Software or the source code into other software or
     services, whether commercial or non-commercial.

Sample sets and recordings are not covered by this licence; the terms of
whoever created them apply.

Requests for permission can be made by opening an issue at
https://github.com/orgelmaker/JM-Orgue/issues

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. THE AUTHOR SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE
